-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-142828" :question/id #uuid "0216a3da-21af-55ff-95a3-8f032518b2e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-142828" :question/problem "$\\frac{(1-{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta )^{2}}{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the secant-tangent identity:\n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nWe rewrite the given expression using the secant-tangent identity as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(1-{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta )^{2}}{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{(1-(1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ))^{2}}{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{(1-1-{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta )^{2}}{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{(-{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta )^{2}}{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot {tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\cdot {tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\cancel{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }} \\\\  & ={tan}^{2}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1-{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta }={tan}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-142828/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7640012b-79f9-5f6b-a26b-a7f4fe8c0e7b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-142828"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-142839/selection/d5492fae97893c9d7eb1044c5d3f4d2e7503ccbbf76e90ffcdfba2316908587d" :answer/id #uuid "9c211ca5-ddc8-5c40-b1dd-ec5b2191f1ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142839/selection/50504bc3966f013136f96678f57cdcbf8c865f016cfe9862c5965714b6200b85" :answer/id #uuid "b61659b2-28d9-547c-926b-c5b24275a2a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142839/selection/bacb644dcae25d563be168ca23fe4c5c1c8292e9ac2cb504ba4b1b351f9a07de" :answer/id #uuid "4116984e-02d3-5b9d-96ae-85752c7b4bed" :answer/type :answer.ty