r-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-120631" :question/id #uuid "c8899a82-fde3-5944-a023-fb73a996cbeb" :question/math-academy-id "q-120631" :question/problem "$\\frac{1}{(1-{cos}^{2}⁡x)(1+{tan}^{2}⁡x)}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the secant-tangent identity:\n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nWe rewrite the given expression using the secant-tangent identity as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{(1-{cos}^{2}⁡x)(1+{tan}^{2}⁡x)} & =\\frac{1}{(1-{cos}^{2}⁡x)\\cdot ({sec}^{2}⁡x)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNext, we recall the following identities:\n\n$$\n1-{cos}^{2}⁡x={sin}^{2}⁡x,\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},\\,\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\n$$\n\n \n\nUsing the above identities, we can further simplify our expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{(1-{cos}^{2}⁡x)\\cdot ({sec}^{2}⁡x)} & =\\frac{1}{({sin}^{2}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{tan}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & ={cot}^{2}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{(1-{cos}^{2}⁡x)(1+{tan}^{2}⁡x)}={cot}^{2}⁡x.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-120631/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "91100afb-9a36-57c0-9f30-4692cfef0b93"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-120631"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-142878/selection/8c3bf13fcf9300cb0afaf9334a6c90848f37134262e7bcd3c72f7b2c9b3cf3cd" :answer/id #uuid "300ce1b6-4b06-5117-8a16-0a33d700a96a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{cos}^{2}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142878/selection/02c776c73871b4dccfdfdf9f1de0c6e6681856b390530f9f76069de4c7ff177b" :answer/id #uuid "4351fc6a-36a9-5