\begin{aligned}(1-{sec}^{2}⁡x)\\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡x & =(1-(1+{tan}^{2}⁡x))\\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =-{tan}^{2}⁡x\\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we recall the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\n$$\n\n \n\nUsing the above identity, we can further simplify our expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{tan}^{2}⁡x\\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡x & =-\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\cancel{{cos}^{2}⁡x}}\\cdot \\cancel{{cos}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =-{sin}^{2}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n(1-{sec}^{2}\\,x)\\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡x=-{sin}^{2}⁡x.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-142878/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "91100afb-9a36-57c0-9f30-4692cfef0b93"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-142878"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-142871/selection/33f84dac408867e4a6524943ad44443f79437696496e99d4e90c21f9132ec5e2" :answer/id #uuid "bb173f22-b901-594c-9098-7a22ce95fe31" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142871/selection/1d926e86f1dcb102a526c2b326c028bf772415bf585c8e6592a82b40e8382030" :answer/id #uuid "ab6a86c1-39ea-5e34-bfbc-019fa8a78ce9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2-{sin}^{2}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142871/selection/c23d7d5e1aafe7e6f428f7befb51edb7e1a645bd38642bab1f7ad30bd927fd75" :answer/id #uuid "c9f903dd-6b7b-576f-8b51-c4520d2cd6da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142871/selection/458a8842e11a3ed75d0854d3b366c95ba71366660083e3e6c7deec5ba83dc00f" :answer/id #uuid "c2b50e4d-22c6-5782-8985-be8bb71d8549" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+2{sin}^{2}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142871/selection/002bd5bf7f826a5414b2ce1dd661bc44bddd9bc46a9710b2cf67db3f6aa5f531" :answer/id #uuid "a1d2cc8d-fff3-57ee-92a8-904346f981ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142871/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ef1f986b-1abe-50ab-91ce-ffb1d2569c28" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-142871/selection/002bd5bf7f826a5414b2ce1dd661bc44bddd9bc46a9710b2cf67db3f6aa5f531" :answer-field/choices ["q-142871/selection/33f84dac408867e4a6524943ad44443f79437696496e99d4e90c21f9132ec5e2" "q-142871/selection/1d926e86f1dcb102a526c2b326c028bf772415bf585c8e6592a82b40e8382030" "q-142871/selection/c23d7d5e1aafe7e6f428f7befb51edb7e1a645bd38642bab1f7ad30bd927fd75" "q-142871/selection/458a8842e11a3ed75d0854d3b366c95ba71366660083e3e6c7deec5ba83dc00f" "q-142871/selection/002bd5bf7f826a5414b2ce1dd661bc44bddd9bc46a9710b2cf67db3f6aa5f531"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-142871" :question/id #uuid "61af6545-1a96-5743-b430-8e3ad4b8da4d" :question/math-academy-id "q-142871" :question/problem "${cos}^{2}⁡x\\text{ }\\,({sec}^{2}⁡x-2{tan}^{2}⁡x)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the secant-tangent identity:\n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe rewrite the given expression using the secant-tangent identity as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡x\\text{ }\\,({sec}^{2}⁡x-2{tan}^{2}⁡x) & ={cos}^{2}⁡x\\text{ }\\,(1+{tan}^{2}⁡x-2{tan}^{2}⁡x) \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡x(1-{tan}^{2}⁡x) \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡x-{cos}^{2}⁡x\\cdot {tan}^{2}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we recall the identities:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},\\,{cos}^{2}⁡x=1-{sin}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\n \n\nUsing the above identities, we can further simplify our expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡x-{cos}^{2}⁡x\\cdot {tan}^{2}⁡x & ={cos}^{2}⁡x-{cos}^{2}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡x-\\cancel{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\cancel{{cos}^{2}⁡x}} \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x\\text{ }\\,({sec}^{2}⁡x-2{tan}^{2}⁡x)=1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-142871/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "91100afb-9a36-57c0-9f30-4692cfef0b93"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-142871"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-120651/selection/45ba5db4c4017ee3a1bce229a169f875d8313fcbc76b4d72f60083f66b0ba711" :answer/id #uuid "d50eb8bd-ddbd-553f-ad34-fd6713a4412a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120651/selection/cfb6bea0eb44d18f6c5766f9b44effcaed90ecc8c07724edbb78ab4c3b462272" :answer/id #uuid "17bc3e17-e07d-51c4-8956-02dbcc3ddc10" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120651/selection/600a97bfe5c0f5f450e278dad500ed1bd1542ae6fbac5348b9d39cec0165c3d5" :answer/id #uuid "2bb8c104-6231-5b9a-b6dc-ad74a7ad86b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120651/selection/619d89e96a97634085e0708b9c9fb875b0dce8a4185996ff1679e8689ab5b971" :answer/id #uuid "8df093f7-9d2b-55a3-81f5-6c3898f28d3d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120651/selection/766aa078e7c29dc2d508d7c6f7ce07c373bbda4e4e81dd53ce2b14d7c3758625" :answer/id #uuid "e9bb77dc-48c4-5d8d-a842-5b38abc68ef7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120651/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e1419d8f-0e0e-512d-b217-ef5f5049d44c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-120651/selection/619d89e96a97634085e0708b9c9fb875b0dce8a4185996ff1679e8689ab5b971" :answer-field/choices ["q-120651/selection/45ba5db4c4017ee3a1bce229a169f875d8313fcbc76b4d72f60083f66b0ba711" "q-120651/selection/cfb6bea0eb44d18f6c5766f9b44effcaed90ecc8c07724edbb78ab4c3b462272" "q-120651/selection/600a97bfe5c0f5f450e278dad500ed1bd1542ae6fbac5348b9d39cec0165c3d5" "q-120651/selection/619d89e96a97634085e0708b9c9fb875b0dce8a4185996ff1679e8689ab5b971" "q-120651/selection/766aa078e7c29dc2d508d7c6f7ce07c373bbda4e4e81dd53ce2b14d7c3758625"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-120651" :question/id #uuid "9b0ff6e0-8d93-5dab-8902-8d6dc2a4a232" :question/math-academy-id "q-120651" :question/problem "$\\frac{{sec}^{3}⁡\\theta \\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the secant-tangent identity:\n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nWe rewrite the given expression using the secant-tangent identity as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{sec}^{3}⁡\\theta \\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }=\\frac{{sec}^{3}⁡\\theta \\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta }\n$$\n\nWe now simplify the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{sec}^{3}⁡\\theta \\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta \\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{{sec}^{2}}\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta \\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\cancel{{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta }} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta \\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we recall the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\n$$\n\n \n\nUsing the above identity, we can further simplify our expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta \\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }}\\cdot \\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{sec}^{3}⁡\\theta \\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-120651/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "91100afb-9a36-57c0-9f30-4692cfef0b93"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-120651"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
